WEBVTT

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.909
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:37.663 --> 00:39.956
I'm not someone
who will leave in three months,

00:39.957 --> 00:42.667
nor someone who might never come back.

00:42.668 --> 00:44.418
Ms. Song, I want to stay

00:44.419 --> 00:45.462
with you.

00:46.463 --> 00:48.840
No, Haran. So I'll tell you everything.

00:49.591 --> 00:53.094
But to tell you everything precisely,

00:53.095 --> 00:54.804
I need some time.

00:54.805 --> 00:55.847
It won't take long.

00:56.431 --> 00:59.142
I'll tell you everything honestly soon.

00:59.643 --> 01:01.603
So when I do,

01:02.354 --> 01:03.729
please listen to everything.

01:05.607 --> 01:07.191
What if you're not okay?

01:07.192 --> 01:08.818
What if something else happens?

01:08.819 --> 01:11.779
I've been okay, I'm okay now,
and I'll keep being okay.

01:11.780 --> 01:12.781
So…

01:14.366 --> 01:15.367
let's go see

01:18.287 --> 01:20.205
the cherry blossoms in spring.

01:21.081 --> 01:23.749
We'll have shaved ice in summer,

01:23.750 --> 01:25.919
see the autumn leaves in fall,

01:26.753 --> 01:27.963
and in winter…

01:29.798 --> 01:31.550
it would be fun to go snowboarding.

01:38.890 --> 01:40.766
EPISODE 10

01:45.480 --> 01:47.440
I think you dropped your bracelet.

01:48.525 --> 01:49.693
This is yours, right?

01:52.779 --> 01:55.490
Oh. Hey, crybaby Song Haran.

02:15.218 --> 02:17.763
- Let's go.
- Let me return her bracelet.

02:21.058 --> 02:24.019
Oh, no. I'm sorry. Oh…

02:25.270 --> 02:27.689
Get your stuff. I'll do this.

02:29.983 --> 02:31.400
I came to ask you for help.

02:31.401 --> 02:33.319
I really want to protect something,

02:33.320 --> 02:35.780
but to do that, I need my memories.

02:36.865 --> 02:38.949
It's okay. It breaks sometimes.

02:38.950 --> 02:41.411
I've been wearing it for a long time.

02:43.622 --> 02:44.706
I'm sorry.

02:46.083 --> 02:48.626
I'm sorry, I'll get it repaired for you.

02:48.627 --> 02:51.296
It's really fine, Haran.

02:53.799 --> 02:54.882
Excuse me?

02:54.883 --> 02:57.094
Ah. Your name was written on the pen.

02:58.220 --> 02:59.471
That's a pretty name.

03:01.014 --> 03:04.183
- Let's go.
- He seems to be in quite a hurry.

03:04.184 --> 03:05.560
You can go. It's fine.

03:07.562 --> 03:09.106
I'm really sorry…

03:10.982 --> 03:12.275
Why are you so on edge?

03:13.985 --> 03:17.738
No, wait. I'm sorry.
You should hurry home and get some rest.

03:17.739 --> 03:19.449
Did the doctor say you're okay?

03:20.117 --> 03:21.118
Yes, I'm fine.

03:21.618 --> 03:22.661
So let's go.

03:37.467 --> 03:40.554
If you feel dizzy or uncomfortable,
tell me straightaway.

03:48.562 --> 03:49.563
Sir.

03:50.063 --> 03:52.441
I'm sorry, but can you pull over nearby?

03:53.608 --> 03:55.277
Shouldn't you get some rest?

03:55.777 --> 03:56.862
I'm totally fine.

03:58.155 --> 04:01.158
Oh? There's a look of doubt on your face.

04:02.117 --> 04:05.369
Then I'll do 100 push-ups!

04:06.455 --> 04:08.414
All right, fine. I believe you.

04:08.415 --> 04:12.294
I feel like we'll just feel down
and regret it if we go home now.

04:12.794 --> 04:13.878
So…

04:15.672 --> 04:19.426
let's begin Seonu Chan's
birthday gift ceremony.

04:22.429 --> 04:24.139
That's my present, right?

04:25.015 --> 04:26.432
This…

04:26.433 --> 04:27.684
Oh… Let me guess.

04:28.268 --> 04:31.062
Mmm… It's clothes.

04:31.772 --> 04:35.192
A cardigan you designed yourself.

04:35.817 --> 04:37.568
How did you know?

04:37.569 --> 04:39.028
I prepared this in secret.

04:39.029 --> 04:40.905
It was obvious.

04:40.906 --> 04:42.032
It was?

04:43.158 --> 04:45.202
Oh. I see…

04:46.578 --> 04:49.331
Hang on. Just give me five minutes.

04:51.208 --> 04:57.546
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

04:57.547 --> 05:01.008
♪ Happy birthday, dear Seonu Chan ♪

05:01.009 --> 05:03.177
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

05:04.596 --> 05:06.055
Wait.

05:06.056 --> 05:07.973
You should still make a wish

05:07.974 --> 05:10.893
even if it's just a humble
convenience store cake.

05:10.894 --> 05:12.562
Then make a wish with me.

05:25.075 --> 05:27.076
Wow!

05:27.077 --> 05:28.328
What did you wish for?

05:28.912 --> 05:31.747
It's a secret.
If I share it, it won't come true.

05:31.748 --> 05:33.290
Right.

05:33.291 --> 05:35.167
Then…

05:35.168 --> 05:37.920
I'll give you your birthday present now.

05:37.921 --> 05:40.257
- Happy birthday.
- Oh. Can I open it right now?

05:48.181 --> 05:49.515
Huh?

05:49.516 --> 05:52.476
I didn't know about this.

05:52.477 --> 05:54.521
At least
I kept one thing a secret.

05:57.107 --> 05:58.358
I'm glad I was born.

06:00.110 --> 06:02.320
Song Haran wished me happy birthday.

06:04.030 --> 06:07.075
Everybody!
Song Haran wished me happy birthday!

06:07.993 --> 06:09.869
Are you crazy?

06:11.121 --> 06:14.915
I'll wear this every day,
in spring, summer, fall, and winter.

06:14.916 --> 06:17.001
I'll wear this to bed, too.

06:17.002 --> 06:20.714
Ah. And even when I'm showering.

06:21.590 --> 06:24.968
I wanted to do more for you
since it's our first birthday together.

06:28.346 --> 06:29.890
Since you seem upset,

06:30.599 --> 06:31.682
how about a date tomorrow?

06:31.683 --> 06:34.685
We can watch a movie,
have a nice meal, hold hands,

06:34.686 --> 06:37.021
and take a walk while we chat.

06:37.022 --> 06:38.690
We'll do what other couples do.

06:39.774 --> 06:42.360
You should just rest. I'm worried.

06:42.944 --> 06:46.572
You leave me
no choice, then. I should do push-ups…

06:46.573 --> 06:49.575
All right. Let's go on a date.

06:50.910 --> 06:55.665
But can you sing that part again?

06:56.541 --> 06:57.875
The…

06:57.876 --> 07:00.754
"dear Seonu Chan" part.

07:03.381 --> 07:06.008
I'll make your birthday
even more special next year.

07:06.009 --> 07:09.262
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

07:14.434 --> 07:15.435
So…

07:16.936 --> 07:18.688
stay healthy, okay?

07:26.863 --> 07:28.323
I will.

07:29.449 --> 07:30.575
Besides,

07:31.159 --> 07:34.079
my mind's filled with you, Haran,

07:35.372 --> 07:38.041
so a tiny fragment in my brain…

07:38.958 --> 07:41.002
won't affect me.

07:55.934 --> 07:57.184
Sir?

07:57.185 --> 07:58.478
Just a moment.

08:12.492 --> 08:13.827
What?

08:14.536 --> 08:15.620
Why are we…

08:17.664 --> 08:19.833
We were in Chuncheon earlier…

08:24.546 --> 08:25.755
Manjae.

08:27.215 --> 08:29.592
We're here. Let's get off.

08:41.563 --> 08:42.814
How long has it been?

08:43.440 --> 08:44.691
Where were you planning

08:46.151 --> 08:47.819
to disappear off to alone?

08:48.737 --> 08:49.821
Manjae.

08:51.614 --> 08:52.699
What do I do?

08:54.909 --> 08:56.244
What do I do about the kids?

09:00.749 --> 09:01.750
I want

09:02.834 --> 09:05.128
to stay with them longer.

09:07.964 --> 09:10.759
I want to stay with you longer, too.

09:12.677 --> 09:14.554
But what if I forget everything?

09:16.765 --> 09:19.267
If I end up
forgetting you and the kids…

09:23.646 --> 09:25.940
and everything else…

09:29.235 --> 09:30.361
I'm scared.

09:31.154 --> 09:32.697
I'm terrified.

09:38.703 --> 09:39.704
It's all right.

09:40.330 --> 09:41.748
Everything will be okay.

09:42.874 --> 09:46.044
You can let it all out with me.

09:48.004 --> 09:49.005
Don't worry.

09:49.714 --> 09:50.840
I will never

09:51.716 --> 09:52.967
let you be alone.

09:54.803 --> 09:56.053
Never.

10:14.447 --> 10:16.991
There's one missing.

10:23.748 --> 10:24.832
Huh?

10:28.461 --> 10:31.256
I took one of her charms.

10:31.840 --> 10:33.216
How do I get this back to her?

10:37.554 --> 10:40.140
The shrapnel's still lodged deep
in the temporal bone.

10:52.902 --> 10:54.112
It's really fine,

10:54.696 --> 10:55.697
Haran.

11:05.540 --> 11:06.749
What did you wish for?

11:07.709 --> 11:10.170
I won't wish for anything else
for the rest of my life.

11:11.087 --> 11:13.380
Please just let me stay with this person

11:13.381 --> 11:15.883
who let me live again,

11:15.884 --> 11:19.345
through every tear and every smile.

11:19.888 --> 11:22.640
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

11:23.183 --> 11:25.059
Just allow me this one thing.

11:25.977 --> 11:28.062
Let me keep staying by her side.

11:48.208 --> 11:53.671
My birthday, the day I decided
to explain everything,

11:54.422 --> 11:55.840
despite the gaps.

12:12.857 --> 12:14.776
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

12:18.738 --> 12:20.531
PETROUS PART OF THE TEMPORAL BONE

12:22.325 --> 12:24.911
Your sister's coming in.

12:26.412 --> 12:27.746
What?

12:27.747 --> 12:29.998
Are you applying for medical school, too?

12:29.999 --> 12:31.416
I was just looking up something.

12:31.417 --> 12:32.584
Is Grandma still sleeping?

12:32.585 --> 12:36.546
Yeah, it's the first time.
She never slept in, even on the weekends.

12:36.547 --> 12:39.300
Is she tired
after her trip to Chuncheon?

12:39.926 --> 12:41.343
But what are those books for?

12:41.344 --> 12:44.638
I just thought I'd work
to get my mind off things.

12:44.639 --> 12:48.267
Do you have the pigment book?
It wasn't in Grandma's study.

12:48.268 --> 12:51.020
It's probably in the attic. Hmm…

12:52.021 --> 12:53.856
Why are your eyes puffy? Did you cry?

12:54.732 --> 12:56.275
Huh?

12:56.276 --> 12:58.819
Of course not.
I just slept well.

12:58.820 --> 13:00.822
Just go and find that book for me.

13:03.074 --> 13:04.200
Thank you.

13:15.336 --> 13:16.963
You can overcome it.

13:18.047 --> 13:20.133
You'll be able to escape on your own.

13:20.925 --> 13:22.426
I wanted to show you, too.

13:31.477 --> 13:34.604
What are you doing?
Why did you pull up your sleeves?

13:34.605 --> 13:36.606
I want to clear out some stuff.

13:36.607 --> 13:37.983
Like a spring deep clean.

13:37.984 --> 13:41.487
Get your head together.
It's the middle of winter.

13:42.530 --> 13:45.366
No, it's spring.

13:51.205 --> 13:53.750
I don't think I'll wear this.

13:55.835 --> 13:57.045
And this…

14:09.265 --> 14:11.142
- I'm heading out.
- Wait.

14:11.726 --> 14:13.602
-  You've got mail.
- Oh?

14:13.603 --> 14:16.563
He must have sent a letter
since it's so hard to reach you.

14:16.564 --> 14:19.191
That poor Kang Hyeokchan.

14:19.192 --> 14:20.776
- See you later.
- Huh?

14:20.777 --> 14:22.862
You're right. Oh…

14:24.322 --> 14:25.323
Yes?

14:25.865 --> 14:27.533
I'll be there right away.

14:38.294 --> 14:41.338
Haran, you must still be busy.

14:41.339 --> 14:44.716
It's already been a month
since I came to Boston.

14:44.717 --> 14:46.968
Everything still feels unfamiliar to me.

14:46.969 --> 14:50.722
I miss you, but it's hard to hear
your voice because of the time difference.

14:50.723 --> 14:52.974
I've been thinking
about a way to communicate.

14:52.975 --> 14:54.893
Can you use a messenger at work?

14:54.894 --> 14:55.937
Tell me if you can.

14:56.604 --> 14:57.939
Ah. Let me tell you something cool.

14:58.523 --> 15:00.816
My dorm roommate is Korean,

15:00.817 --> 15:02.359
and his name's Chan, too.

15:02.360 --> 15:03.528
Isn't that funny?

15:04.195 --> 15:06.655
But I think it'll be hard
to get close to him.

15:06.656 --> 15:08.741
He seems a bit closed off.

15:09.325 --> 15:11.159
I miss you so much, Haran.

15:11.160 --> 15:13.328
I'll come see you during summer break.

15:13.329 --> 15:15.414
Take care. I love you.

15:20.795 --> 15:23.505
I booked the movie tickets.
I'll see you at 5:00 p.m.

15:23.506 --> 15:25.466
Oh. I should get ready.

15:39.647 --> 15:40.856
Mr. Park.

15:40.857 --> 15:43.776
I might come home pretty late tonight.

15:46.612 --> 15:48.488
All right.

15:48.489 --> 15:51.324
Talk it out with Haran.

15:51.325 --> 15:55.329
If you're sincere,
I'm sure she'll understand.

16:00.126 --> 16:02.170
- All right. I will.
- Okay.

16:15.016 --> 16:16.641
They must be in the corner.

16:16.642 --> 16:19.812
This is broken.
It won't charge.

16:27.695 --> 16:30.114
Do you have time
after the movie?

16:31.449 --> 16:33.367
There's something I have to tell you.

16:34.368 --> 16:37.622
I'll tell you everything honestly soon.

16:39.582 --> 16:40.791
All right.

16:42.543 --> 16:45.003
Oh? I forgot the other popcorn.

16:45.004 --> 16:46.713
I'll go get it.

16:46.714 --> 16:49.050
- Just wait here.
- I'll wait inside, then.

17:01.604 --> 17:03.606
-  Sorry about that.
- It's okay.

17:04.106 --> 17:05.107
Thank you.

17:09.070 --> 17:11.112
- Is it a false alarm?
- What do we do?

17:11.113 --> 17:13.699
Please follow the instructions
and evacuate immediately.

17:14.325 --> 17:15.408
Please don't push.

17:15.409 --> 17:16.452
Song Haran.

17:17.787 --> 17:18.913
Please go downstairs.

17:19.747 --> 17:21.331
Don't push!

17:25.962 --> 17:27.672
Evacuate immediately.

17:29.423 --> 17:31.132
You shouldn't go inside.

17:31.133 --> 17:32.217
Sorry!

17:32.218 --> 17:33.344
- Sir!
- Song Haran!

17:34.595 --> 17:35.887
Song Haran!

17:45.648 --> 17:47.108
Stop it!

17:59.787 --> 18:00.997
Seonu Chan!

18:03.541 --> 18:05.501
Seonu Chan!

18:06.002 --> 18:07.085
I'll tell you everything.

18:07.086 --> 18:10.338
I'll tell you about the scars on my body.

18:10.339 --> 18:12.550
I don't do well in noisy places.

18:14.218 --> 18:16.304
Seonu Chan! Where are you?

18:23.102 --> 18:25.353
Where were you?

18:25.354 --> 18:26.730
I couldn't see you outside,

18:26.731 --> 18:28.649
- so I thought you'd gone inside…
- I'm okay.

18:29.317 --> 18:32.069
I'm so relieved nothing happened.

18:36.616 --> 18:37.825
It's okay.

18:38.576 --> 18:40.243
Let's go to the hospital
and get you checked.

18:40.244 --> 18:42.330
I'll get a checkup soon.

18:42.830 --> 18:44.457
Don't worry.

18:45.666 --> 18:47.543
I'll be completely fine.

18:57.303 --> 18:59.304
MEDICAL CHECKUP

19:02.642 --> 19:03.975
Grandma.

19:03.976 --> 19:06.103
What is it, Haran? Is something wrong?

19:11.150 --> 19:12.275
What do I do, Grandma?

19:13.569 --> 19:15.696
He's not well.

19:16.906 --> 19:18.783
He keeps collapsing,

19:19.784 --> 19:21.869
and there's something lodged in his head.

19:22.662 --> 19:25.164
He says he's okay,
but he doesn't seem okay at all.

19:26.290 --> 19:28.918
What do I do
if something happens to him?

19:30.169 --> 19:32.128
I may not be

19:32.129 --> 19:35.883
as good for her as you believe.

19:42.807 --> 19:44.475
He's not keeping it from you.

19:45.184 --> 19:46.352
He probably can't

19:47.144 --> 19:48.145
because he's scared.

19:48.813 --> 19:51.399
He probably doesn't want
to burden you with his pain

19:52.066 --> 19:53.525
because it would hurt you.

19:53.526 --> 19:54.652
He cares more

19:55.486 --> 19:57.946
about protecting you than his own pain.

19:57.947 --> 19:59.990
But I want to protect him.

20:01.158 --> 20:03.327
I don't want him to go through it alone.

20:04.578 --> 20:07.038
But there's nothing I can do for him.

20:07.039 --> 20:08.749
Just stay by his side.

20:09.458 --> 20:13.379
People can stay strong
even with just one person by their side.

20:13.921 --> 20:14.964
Trust me, I know.

20:16.090 --> 20:18.758
So don't worry too much.

20:18.759 --> 20:21.637
I'm sure you'll find a way.

20:38.279 --> 20:39.280
Waste container…

20:39.905 --> 20:41.073
Kang Hyeokchan…

20:41.657 --> 20:42.700
Lab…

20:43.451 --> 20:44.701
Cha Sujin…

20:47.371 --> 20:48.497
Stop it!

20:49.165 --> 20:50.332
And me…

20:51.834 --> 20:53.586
Was that day…

20:57.757 --> 21:00.592
"Volatile reagent container fractured…"

21:00.593 --> 21:02.302
"Self-reactive event

21:02.303 --> 21:05.097
triggered by careless handling
of reagents."

21:05.598 --> 21:09.142
"The cause has not been
conclusively determined."

21:09.143 --> 21:10.226
No, there's nothing.

21:10.227 --> 21:11.853
I said I don't know!

21:13.647 --> 21:17.443
What is she trying to hide?

21:25.242 --> 21:27.160
Don't do anything tomorrow

21:27.161 --> 21:29.078
and get plenty of rest.

21:29.079 --> 21:30.873
I'll always be by your side.

21:38.672 --> 21:42.301
MY BIRTHDAY, THE DAY I DECIDED
TO EXPLAIN EVERYTHING, DESPITE THE GAPS

21:45.262 --> 21:47.807
KANG HYEOKCHAN
CHA SUJIN

21:59.735 --> 22:01.737
12-WEEK REHABILITATION PLAN

22:02.279 --> 22:04.490
Ah. It's tomorrow.

22:05.074 --> 22:09.369
But, Mr. Park, when should we tell
Hadam and her sisters?

22:09.370 --> 22:10.870
Yougyum!

22:10.871 --> 22:12.330
Hey, Dad!

22:12.331 --> 22:13.498
Really? Okay.

22:13.499 --> 22:15.041
Is it your dad?

22:15.042 --> 22:16.710
- Let me say hi.
- Okay, Dad.

22:17.336 --> 22:19.839
I said I wanted to say hi.

22:20.881 --> 22:22.591
Oh, I didn't hear you.

22:23.634 --> 22:25.427
- Sorry.
- Gosh.

22:26.804 --> 22:28.888
Ta-da. It's pumpkin porridge.

22:28.889 --> 22:32.768
It's rich in beta-carotene and vitamin A,
so it'll help with the inflammation.

22:33.352 --> 22:34.687
Make sure to eat everything.

22:43.612 --> 22:45.489
- Hadam.
- Yes?

22:46.073 --> 22:48.324
You know I like you so, so much, right?

22:48.325 --> 22:50.452
You helped me stay strong
when I was in pain.

22:51.203 --> 22:53.621
If you ever have a hard time someday,

22:53.622 --> 22:57.208
I'll do the same for you
so that you stay strong.

22:57.209 --> 22:59.335
Sure.

22:59.336 --> 23:02.046
But that's not going to happen.

23:02.047 --> 23:04.674
Once you're better,
I'll have nothing but happy days ahead.

23:27.573 --> 23:28.740
Hi.

23:28.741 --> 23:31.284
- Did you have a good weekend?
- Yes.

23:31.285 --> 23:33.286
I'm on my way to meet Mr. Chae.

23:33.287 --> 23:36.289
He sent me files on the material,
but they kept getting corrupted,

23:36.290 --> 23:37.749
so he's bringing them in person.

23:37.750 --> 23:39.501
He must have something to cover nearby.

23:40.586 --> 23:42.503
That's quite a coincidence.

23:45.424 --> 23:49.052
Ah. I was checking the sample dye
from the color team.

23:49.053 --> 23:50.512
I guess it wasn't dry yet.

23:51.555 --> 23:53.223
I'll get going, then.

23:55.517 --> 23:58.562
I felt so awkward
I ended up rambling.

24:10.032 --> 24:12.825
Um… These are the colors
that Ms. Kim directed.

24:12.826 --> 24:15.578
Then this would be the most similar,

24:15.579 --> 24:18.331
but it might look muted on the fabric.

24:18.332 --> 24:19.457
I think so, too.

24:19.458 --> 24:21.459
We should try mixing the colors again.

24:21.460 --> 24:24.420
Then let's apply the feedback
and submit a report for now.

24:24.421 --> 24:26.506
Okay.

24:26.507 --> 24:27.715
Coffee?

24:27.716 --> 24:29.425
All right, everyone.

24:29.426 --> 24:31.386
Fresh coffee.

24:31.387 --> 24:33.262
- Mr. Park.
- Hello.

24:33.263 --> 24:34.514
What brings you here?

24:34.515 --> 24:36.474
I got a new batch of beans.

24:36.475 --> 24:37.725
Gosh.

24:37.726 --> 24:41.855
So I thought I'd deliver some
to my regular customers.

24:42.523 --> 24:44.273
Thank you.

24:44.274 --> 24:46.609
-  No problem.
- I'm taking this one.

24:46.610 --> 24:48.319
It's totally my style.

24:48.320 --> 24:49.946
Oh, I'm sorry.

24:49.947 --> 24:53.241
This is reserved for someone else.

24:53.242 --> 24:55.118
- Take this.
- Okay.

24:56.412 --> 24:58.705
Too bad. Ribbons are my signature.

25:01.083 --> 25:04.460
You brought coffee for everyone
since it'll be too obvious, right?

25:04.461 --> 25:05.795
Oh…

25:05.796 --> 25:07.630
- Could you tell?
- Yes.

25:10.009 --> 25:11.676
How was your trip to Chuncheon?

25:11.677 --> 25:13.970
Grandma was so excited to go.

25:13.971 --> 25:16.723
Uh… Of course.

25:16.724 --> 25:17.808
We had a great time.

25:19.226 --> 25:21.728
By the way, is Mr. Seonu okay?

25:21.729 --> 25:23.813
I didn't call
since I didn't want to bother him.

25:23.814 --> 25:26.442
What? Did something happen?

25:27.026 --> 25:30.279
He clearly doesn't seem well,
but he won't tell me.

25:33.115 --> 25:35.825
Some people have a hard time

25:35.826 --> 25:38.245
sharing things when they care
about someone deeply.

25:40.372 --> 25:41.874
I can guarantee you

25:42.416 --> 25:46.419
that when Chan
really has to tell you something,

25:46.420 --> 25:48.047
he'll tell you honestly

25:48.922 --> 25:50.548
without hiding it.

25:51.759 --> 25:55.345
So just trust him
and wait patiently for that moment.

25:57.598 --> 25:58.599
All right.

26:00.392 --> 26:01.393
Mmm.

26:05.022 --> 26:06.774
I startled you in Chuncheon, didn't I?

26:07.357 --> 26:10.068
I was startled too and acted like a child.

26:10.069 --> 26:11.152
I'm sorry.

26:11.153 --> 26:13.739
But you don't have to worry.

26:14.698 --> 26:16.407
I already planned everything.

26:16.408 --> 26:18.827
What plan? To disappear on your own?

26:20.662 --> 26:22.164
Your checkup's tomorrow, right?

26:23.373 --> 26:25.542
You have to take me with you.

26:26.418 --> 26:28.920
How did you know the date?

26:28.921 --> 26:30.546
I met Yougyum.

26:30.547 --> 26:34.550
He told me about the necklace
and how he's the only one who knows.

26:36.720 --> 26:37.970
I see.

26:37.971 --> 26:41.682
But I'm not a child, you know.

26:41.683 --> 26:43.936
- I can go by myself--
- Nabong.

26:45.062 --> 26:47.981
You don't have to act tough
in front of me.

26:50.067 --> 26:51.110
I told you,

26:52.444 --> 26:54.446
I won't let you be alone.

26:58.784 --> 26:59.952
I guess this is why

27:01.453 --> 27:02.955
we met after 50 years.

27:04.706 --> 27:07.626
You have no one to rely on,
and have so many things to protect.

27:10.379 --> 27:11.588
I'll protect you,

27:13.298 --> 27:14.383
so you can rely on me.

27:15.384 --> 27:17.052
I'll stay by your side.

27:31.483 --> 27:32.568
Hmm?

27:35.112 --> 27:37.239
What is all this?

27:40.075 --> 27:42.785
You have to handle
everything on the desk in my place.

27:42.786 --> 27:43.911
Finish them by today.

27:46.540 --> 27:48.082
Hello? Ms. Kim--

27:48.083 --> 27:51.043
Among the 12 SS candidate outfits,
the six I picked are fixed.

27:51.044 --> 27:53.170
Pick the other six.

27:53.171 --> 27:56.716
Submit a report on which to pick
and the reasons by today.

27:56.717 --> 27:58.217
What? But--

27:58.218 --> 28:00.428
You saw the pigment samples
yesterday, right?

28:00.429 --> 28:03.431
Organize the differences in color
and decide which one to go with.

28:03.432 --> 28:06.058
And the differences by fabric.
Send it by today.

28:06.059 --> 28:07.810
Wait, Ms. Kim. I--

28:07.811 --> 28:10.771
I received two drafts
of the press kit for Paris.

28:10.772 --> 28:13.649
Choose the one that suits our image
and give it to Mr. Yeon.

28:13.650 --> 28:16.611
I have work outside the office,
so I won't be there today.

28:16.612 --> 28:19.113
Finish everything by today
and send it to me by email.

28:19.114 --> 28:22.241
- All of that by today?
- Are you saying you can't?

28:22.242 --> 28:24.076
Did you forget?
I told you to take my workload.

28:24.077 --> 28:25.579
But still, this is…

28:31.209 --> 28:32.294
Mr. Park!

28:40.052 --> 28:42.971
Hmm?
He didn't mention anything.

28:44.598 --> 28:45.599
Genius.

28:47.726 --> 28:50.145
Do you know where Mr. Park went?

28:51.271 --> 28:52.272
Hmm?

28:53.398 --> 28:55.233
Where did he go?

28:57.486 --> 29:01.073
Ms. Kim, can you confirm the materials…

29:01.698 --> 29:02.782
Ah…

29:02.783 --> 29:04.533
Right, she's at a meeting.

29:04.534 --> 29:05.577
Okay.

29:08.914 --> 29:11.708
I can't believe this.
Hayeong, you klutz.

29:14.503 --> 29:15.545
Goodness.

29:16.296 --> 29:17.297
What is this?

29:20.550 --> 29:23.135
DON'T CAUSE TROUBLE FOR MY GRANDDAUGHTERS
I'M STILL OKAY

29:23.136 --> 29:25.054
KEEP GLASSES IN FRONT OF THE MONITOR

29:25.055 --> 29:27.098
DON'T TAKE OFF YOUGYUM'S NECKLACE!

29:29.851 --> 29:32.479
"Noble Life Center"?

29:40.445 --> 29:42.406
NOBLE LIFE CENTER
COUNSELING CENTER

29:46.994 --> 29:48.327
Secure retirement.

29:48.328 --> 29:51.498
This is the Noble Life Center,
Korea's premium senior care center.

29:52.207 --> 29:54.584
Hello, this is Noble Life Center.

29:55.711 --> 29:57.629
I…

29:59.381 --> 30:00.382
I mean,

30:01.925 --> 30:02.926
I wanted

30:03.760 --> 30:07.430
to check my reservation.

30:07.431 --> 30:08.598
What is your name?

30:10.851 --> 30:14.270
I'm Kim Nabong's guardian.

30:14.271 --> 30:15.896
Right, Kim Nabong.

30:15.897 --> 30:18.483
She's still set to move in
at the end of June, right?

30:19.234 --> 30:21.193
You wanted a single room

30:21.194 --> 30:23.738
and signed up for the specialized
dementia care, right?

30:23.739 --> 30:26.408
CLOSET KEY, JEWELRY BOX

30:27.325 --> 30:28.994
"Closet key, jewelry box…"

30:44.718 --> 30:46.969
I really don't need lunch.

30:46.970 --> 30:49.848
When do I finish all of this?

30:55.353 --> 30:56.605
Hayeong.

30:59.775 --> 31:01.150
What is it?

31:01.151 --> 31:03.028
What's wrong? Huh?

31:04.112 --> 31:06.031
What do we do?

31:06.782 --> 31:08.992
What do we do about Grandma?

31:09.576 --> 31:11.952
What about Grandma? What's going on?

31:16.333 --> 31:17.542
What is this?

31:23.006 --> 31:25.634
NOBLE LIFE CENTER
CALL TO CONFIRM RESERVATION ON THE 17TH!

31:33.141 --> 31:35.852
What do you mean?
Why would she go to a care center?

31:37.187 --> 31:40.940
I know you're just playing a joke
since my CSAT is over.

31:40.941 --> 31:43.276
- Hadam.
- That doesn't make any sense.

31:44.069 --> 31:45.320
Why would Grandma…

31:45.862 --> 31:48.572
Why would she go there?

31:48.573 --> 31:51.785
I think she was trying
to leave quietly.

31:53.745 --> 31:55.455
She must have been planning it

31:56.206 --> 31:58.083
for quite a long time.

32:27.154 --> 32:28.738
This was in here.

32:41.293 --> 32:43.211
To my beloved granddaughters.

32:43.795 --> 32:47.548
Bonjour, my beautiful granddaughters
who took after me.

32:47.549 --> 32:49.675
By the time you've opened this,

32:49.676 --> 32:52.553
I'll probably be having champagne

32:52.554 --> 32:54.556
on a plane to southern France.

32:55.640 --> 32:57.099
Don't move, ma'am.

32:57.100 --> 32:59.352
Don't be too upset.

32:59.978 --> 33:04.106
I want to reward myself
for working hard all these years.

33:04.107 --> 33:06.025
So I'm really happy.

33:06.026 --> 33:08.527
-  Please curl your back.
-  Oh.

33:08.528 --> 33:11.697
And don't try to visit me.

33:11.698 --> 33:14.074
I had such a hard time in my 20s

33:14.075 --> 33:16.493
attending fashion school
with a baby on my back.

33:16.494 --> 33:18.371
And I didn't get to try so many things

33:18.955 --> 33:21.791
because I had no money or time.

33:22.292 --> 33:26.713
I'm going to be extremely busy
doing everything I couldn't do back then.

33:27.631 --> 33:29.006
So please…

33:29.007 --> 33:30.299
-  Ms. Kim Nabong.
- Yes.

33:30.300 --> 33:32.843
-  Let me enjoy my life here.
- Head to the next room.

33:32.844 --> 33:37.015
Ah. And as for those
wedding gowns…

33:46.775 --> 33:51.320
Your grandma's the famous Kim Nana,

33:51.321 --> 33:54.366
so letting you wear wedding gowns
made by someone else?

33:54.866 --> 33:56.242
Oh, no.

33:56.243 --> 33:57.869
I can never let that happen.

33:59.871 --> 34:02.998
I thought I'd be too busy
having fun in France

34:02.999 --> 34:04.917
to make any clothes,

34:04.918 --> 34:06.253
so I made them in advance.

34:07.003 --> 34:10.340
I just made them easily in my spare time.

34:12.801 --> 34:15.511
Let's meet again someday

34:15.512 --> 34:17.806
after shining in each of our places.

34:18.515 --> 34:22.936
I'll be rooting for your glorious lives
from far away.

34:23.728 --> 34:24.895
Haran,

34:24.896 --> 34:26.481
Hayeong,

34:27.315 --> 34:28.400
Hadam.

34:33.029 --> 34:35.240
My life was a brilliant shade of rose

34:35.907 --> 34:40.287
because you three were my granddaughters.

34:41.621 --> 34:42.622
Take care.

34:43.123 --> 34:44.124
Au revoir.

34:45.166 --> 34:46.250
Ah.

34:46.251 --> 34:50.838
I hate saying cheesy things,
but I'm the type to say things I need to.

34:52.132 --> 34:53.133
I love you,

34:53.800 --> 34:55.760
my dear granddaughters.

34:58.179 --> 34:59.389
Why…

35:00.974 --> 35:03.018
She has three granddaughters.

35:04.269 --> 35:05.519
Why would she…

35:05.520 --> 35:07.188
It's weird that she's at a meeting.

35:08.356 --> 35:09.608
Where is she right now?

35:10.775 --> 35:12.319
She hasn't left already, has she?

35:21.494 --> 35:24.788
SECRET WITH YOUGYUM
DON'T TAKE OFF YOUGYUM'S NECKLACE!

35:26.082 --> 35:28.417
Why don't you spend some time
with your grandma--

35:28.418 --> 35:30.878
Why are you suddenly
bringing up my grandma?

35:30.879 --> 35:31.880
What?

35:32.839 --> 35:33.922
Oh…

35:33.923 --> 35:36.967
Why was your tumbler
in my grandma's study?

35:36.968 --> 35:38.761
I ran into her a while ago in the park.

35:38.762 --> 35:40.889
You know she wouldn't do such a thing.

35:48.146 --> 35:51.858
Cha Yougyum.
You knew about Grandma, didn't you?

35:52.484 --> 35:53.817
Where is she right now?

35:53.818 --> 35:57.155
I already know everything!
Just tell me!

35:58.406 --> 36:00.659
She's getting a checkup today.

36:07.957 --> 36:09.041
Over there.

36:09.042 --> 36:10.960
NEUROLOGY CENTER

36:15.131 --> 36:17.007
-  Oh.
- Hey, Manjae.

36:17.008 --> 36:18.718
- That took a while, didn't it?
-  Goodness.

36:18.843 --> 36:20.135
You did great.

36:20.136 --> 36:21.512
- Are you okay?
-  Yes.

36:29.354 --> 36:30.813
How can you…

36:30.814 --> 36:32.981
Of all people, how can you do this to me?

36:32.982 --> 36:34.608
Why are you--

36:34.609 --> 36:36.527
You should take some of my workload.

36:36.528 --> 36:38.320
Let me get some rest, too.

36:38.321 --> 36:40.864
He's not keeping it from you.
He probably can't.

36:40.865 --> 36:43.659
He probably doesn't want
to burden you with his pain.

36:43.660 --> 36:46.287
He cares more about protecting you
than his own pain.

36:52.711 --> 36:54.002
A meeting?

36:54.003 --> 36:55.504
And what's this…

36:55.505 --> 36:56.506
I'll do it.

37:02.512 --> 37:03.679
What was that, Grandma?

37:03.680 --> 37:06.014
You didn't even look at him
and didn't say a word.

37:06.015 --> 37:08.267
He left because
you made him uncomfortable.

37:08.268 --> 37:11.271
Did Grandma summon you
and threaten you or something?

37:23.533 --> 37:25.493
DON'T CAUSE TROUBLE FOR MY GRANDDAUGHTERS

37:38.465 --> 37:39.466
Grandma.

37:47.974 --> 37:49.100
I'm okay.

37:49.684 --> 37:50.685
It's all right.

37:53.938 --> 37:56.398
Ms. Kim Nabong.
Please go to the next room.

37:56.399 --> 37:57.442
Okay.

37:58.735 --> 38:00.110
I'll be back.

38:00.111 --> 38:01.196
Let's go.

38:10.914 --> 38:13.332
You've a lot of granddaughters.

38:13.333 --> 38:14.833
All right.

38:14.834 --> 38:15.835
See you in a bit.

38:31.851 --> 38:35.813
Make sure to keep it dry,
and tell me if it's too tight.

38:35.814 --> 38:37.065
Okay. Thank you.

38:38.983 --> 38:40.067
Are you okay?

38:40.068 --> 38:41.569
I'm fine.

38:42.737 --> 38:44.988
You need some vitamins.
I'll peel these for you.

38:44.989 --> 38:47.366
- It's fine, I'll do it.
- Mmm-mmm.

38:47.367 --> 38:49.619
- Ah…
-  Cha Yougyum!

38:52.330 --> 38:53.331
Bye.

38:57.126 --> 38:58.127
Hadam…

39:00.880 --> 39:03.340
I'm sorry I didn't tell you
about your grandma.

39:03.341 --> 39:05.009
She said…

39:08.721 --> 39:10.848
Thank you, Yougyum.

39:11.933 --> 39:13.351
Thank you so much.

39:14.477 --> 39:17.646
Yougyum has been taking care of her.

39:17.647 --> 39:19.439
Without the necklace he gave her,

39:19.440 --> 39:22.277
I would've lost her in Chuncheon.

39:23.403 --> 39:26.948
It must have been tough
keeping that secret on his own.

39:27.657 --> 39:30.243
She would've had a hard time on her own.

39:32.036 --> 39:33.037
Thank you

39:33.788 --> 39:35.456
for taking care of her.

39:41.838 --> 39:43.172
Sorry, I didn't tell you.

39:43.715 --> 39:45.133
You must've been shocked.

39:46.551 --> 39:47.552
Thank you.

39:48.887 --> 39:51.306
Thank you so, so much, Yougyum.

39:55.351 --> 39:57.979
Let's go see her.

40:19.292 --> 40:20.293
I didn't know.

40:22.545 --> 40:24.505
I should've known,

40:26.174 --> 40:27.175
but I didn't.

40:27.842 --> 40:28.843
Why?

40:29.385 --> 40:31.429
How could you not know?

40:32.180 --> 40:34.723
It was you of all people.

40:34.724 --> 40:36.225
You said she was your savior,

40:37.060 --> 40:38.769
and you promised to take care of her.

40:38.770 --> 40:41.188
You were always by her side.
How could you not know?

40:43.066 --> 40:45.735
When I asked if anything happened
in Seongsu-dong,

40:46.569 --> 40:47.862
why did you hide it from me?

40:48.738 --> 40:51.073
No, if you weren't going to tell me,

40:51.074 --> 40:53.283
shouldn't you have
looked into it more, at least?

40:53.284 --> 40:55.161
If you'd found out then…

40:56.079 --> 40:57.080
I'm sorry.

40:58.247 --> 40:59.248
No.

41:00.083 --> 41:01.501
Pretend you didn't hear that.

41:02.460 --> 41:03.878
What I just said

41:04.671 --> 41:06.839
is actually what I want to say to myself.

41:09.092 --> 41:11.302
I know it's not your fault,

41:11.886 --> 41:15.974
but I feel so pathetic and stupid.

41:17.475 --> 41:19.727
So I don't know what to do.

41:20.979 --> 41:23.189
I should've known.

41:24.399 --> 41:25.400
I'm sorry…

41:26.275 --> 41:27.527
I yelled at you.

41:38.746 --> 41:39.871
Sorry.

41:46.587 --> 41:47.755
He's not picking up.

41:48.756 --> 41:50.632
Mr. Park, where are you?

41:50.633 --> 41:53.386
Customers are coming in,
asking why you're closed today.

41:55.763 --> 41:56.764
The hospital?

41:58.850 --> 42:00.267
Then what about…

42:00.268 --> 42:02.437
What about Ms. Song?

42:03.062 --> 42:06.231
The MRI shows
normal intracranial pressure,

42:06.232 --> 42:09.317
but the ventricles
are significantly enlarged.

42:09.318 --> 42:11.987
We also ran a cerebrospinal fluid test
to double-check,

42:11.988 --> 42:13.531
and the results show…

42:16.159 --> 42:17.410
that it's not dementia.

42:18.619 --> 42:20.245
Really?

42:20.246 --> 42:21.580
That's such a relief.

42:21.581 --> 42:25.542
But we suspect
normal pressure hydrocephalus.

42:25.543 --> 42:27.210
Hydrocephalus?

42:27.211 --> 42:30.088
It occurs when cerebrospinal fluid
isn't properly absorbed,

42:30.089 --> 42:33.925
leading to symptoms like memory loss
and problems with walking.

42:33.926 --> 42:36.887
The symptoms are similar,
so some mistake it for dementia.

42:36.888 --> 42:38.221
I see.

42:38.222 --> 42:41.059
Have you had any problems
with walking recently?

42:42.185 --> 42:44.937
- I don't think I've seen…
- I'm not sure…

42:45.438 --> 42:46.646
-  Oh!
-  Oh gosh.

42:46.647 --> 42:50.358
She did. Last time,
you had bruises on your legs.

42:50.359 --> 42:52.569
Huh? Did you hit your leg somewhere?

42:52.570 --> 42:55.323
It's fine. I just fell.
My legs suddenly wouldn't listen.

42:56.074 --> 42:58.575
Patients usually show a response
within 24 hours,

42:58.576 --> 43:01.286
even within 10 hours
after draining the cerebrospinal fluid.

43:01.287 --> 43:03.830
We'll be able to confirm this
after the gait test.

43:03.831 --> 43:06.084
So let's see
how much improvement there is.

43:06.876 --> 43:09.628
You can see how you sometimes
had narrower strides

43:09.629 --> 43:12.255
and dragged your feet
in the morning, right?

43:12.256 --> 43:14.801
But it improved significantly
after draining the fluid.

43:15.843 --> 43:18.887
The tap test confirms
normal pressure hydrocephalus.

43:18.888 --> 43:22.516
She can get better
with treatment, right?

43:22.517 --> 43:24.392
With successful surgery,
she should improve.

43:24.393 --> 43:25.894
All right.

43:25.895 --> 43:28.313
We'll create a small opening in the skull

43:28.314 --> 43:31.233
and insert a thin tube called a shunt
into the ventricle

43:31.234 --> 43:34.820
to drain excess cerebrospinal fluid
into the abdomen.

43:34.821 --> 43:36.404
Ah…

43:36.405 --> 43:39.658
Given your age, I suggest
getting hospitalized a few days in advance

43:39.659 --> 43:41.327
to run some basic tests first.

43:41.994 --> 43:43.495
Proceed with the admission,

43:43.496 --> 43:46.832
and we'll set the surgery date
based on your condition.

43:48.376 --> 43:50.877
The admission's done already?

43:50.878 --> 43:55.423
Yes, a tall man in a suit
came and finished the process.

43:55.424 --> 43:56.926
He even paid the fees.

44:00.763 --> 44:01.930
Mr. Yeon.

44:28.124 --> 44:29.249
Cha Yougyum.

44:29.250 --> 44:30.333
Yes, Ms. Kim.

44:30.334 --> 44:34.254
You're an athlete.
Go take care of your own condition.

44:34.255 --> 44:35.505
You need to recover.

44:35.506 --> 44:37.341
- Song Hadam.
- Yes?

44:37.967 --> 44:39.260
You said you'd help him.

44:39.760 --> 44:41.554
Stay right by his side.

44:42.555 --> 44:43.598
And…

44:44.724 --> 44:46.308
Song Haran, Song Hayeong.

44:46.309 --> 44:50.353
No, Lead Designer Song,
Designer Song Hayeong.

44:50.354 --> 44:55.108
If anything at my company
goes wrong while I'm away,

44:55.109 --> 44:56.526
I'm kicking all of you out.

44:56.527 --> 44:58.320
So focus on work from now on.

44:58.321 --> 45:00.572
Don't even think about coming here.

45:00.573 --> 45:01.866
But…

45:02.450 --> 45:03.533
Okay.

45:03.534 --> 45:06.286
I'll be taking care of her
from now on,

45:06.287 --> 45:09.748
so you youngsters
go and focus on your own stuff.

45:09.749 --> 45:12.125
We'll take turns coming here.
You have your coffee shop.

45:12.126 --> 45:13.210
Mmm-mmm.

45:13.211 --> 45:15.587
SHIM is temporarily closed
until she gets surgery

45:15.588 --> 45:18.423
and recovers well.

45:18.424 --> 45:19.966
I'll think of this as winter vacation

45:19.967 --> 45:23.345
and enjoy my time here with my old friend.

45:24.555 --> 45:27.016
All right. Everyone, stop bothering us.

45:28.100 --> 45:30.727
But where did Mr. Yeon go?

45:30.728 --> 45:33.188
- I thought I saw him in the hallway.
-  Oh.

45:33.189 --> 45:35.273
He'll probably be busy
taking care of things

45:35.274 --> 45:36.817
in Grandma's place.

45:46.953 --> 45:47.995
Oh?

45:51.374 --> 45:53.876
I'm sorry, I took so long.

45:54.543 --> 45:55.961
How did you know?

45:55.962 --> 45:58.672
I heard from Mr. Park just a while ago.

45:58.673 --> 46:01.383
I'm sure her surgery will go well.

46:02.635 --> 46:08.182
I wish the people I love won't feel pain,
physically or mentally.

46:08.766 --> 46:10.558
I'm sure she'll overcome this.

46:10.559 --> 46:12.519
So don't get too scared.

46:12.520 --> 46:13.854
Everything will be all right.

46:14.397 --> 46:18.358
Sorry, but can we stay like this
for 10 more seconds?

46:18.359 --> 46:21.821
We can stay like this for 10 minutes
or even 10 hours.

46:22.613 --> 46:25.240
Sorry,
I didn't contact you sooner.

46:25.241 --> 46:26.492
Things were so hectic.

46:27.243 --> 46:28.244
Oh?

46:29.495 --> 46:31.705
I'll be upset if you feel sorry over this.

46:33.416 --> 46:34.709
You must've missed lunch.

46:35.501 --> 46:37.127
Wait here, I'll get you something.

46:37.128 --> 46:41.214
Then can I just get some coffee?
I don't think I can eat anything.

46:41.215 --> 46:43.009
All right. Hang on.

46:43.592 --> 46:46.637
Why are you dressed so lightly?

46:48.431 --> 46:51.808
This cardigan is really valuable to me,

46:51.809 --> 46:54.185
so I don't usually lend it to anyone.

46:54.186 --> 46:56.188
But I'll let you wear it just this once.

47:00.484 --> 47:01.485
Don't ruin it.

47:12.246 --> 47:13.247
We meet again.

47:14.457 --> 47:16.042
Oh. Hello.

47:16.625 --> 47:20.003
My grandma's getting hospitalized here
for a few days.

47:20.004 --> 47:21.464
Ah. Really?

47:22.006 --> 47:25.717
Oh, um… I accidentally took
one of your bracelet charms.

47:25.718 --> 47:27.969
I'll give it back to you
when I visit tomorrow.

47:27.970 --> 47:30.472
Really? I was wondering
where that charm went.

47:30.473 --> 47:32.808
That's great. But…

47:33.351 --> 47:35.144
the man who was with you last time…

47:36.979 --> 47:38.356
Is he your boyfriend?

47:39.190 --> 47:40.774
Yes. Why do you ask?

47:40.775 --> 47:42.151
You looked good together.

47:42.902 --> 47:46.071
He reminded me of someone I used to know.

47:46.072 --> 47:47.782
Ah.

47:48.366 --> 47:50.826
Oh… You're a neurology doctor.

47:51.702 --> 47:54.371
My grandmother's getting surgery
for hydrocephalus.

47:54.372 --> 47:56.039
Please take good care of her.

47:56.040 --> 47:58.959
I'm only visiting, so I'm not authorized
to treat patients directly.

48:01.545 --> 48:02.755
I came from Boston.

48:03.547 --> 48:04.548
Oh.

48:05.091 --> 48:06.466
I see.

48:06.467 --> 48:08.301
The neurosurgeons
will take good care of her.

48:08.302 --> 48:11.430
The neurology department
will see the results, so I'll check.

48:12.014 --> 48:13.349
And my bracelet…

48:14.058 --> 48:15.476
I was worried

48:16.352 --> 48:19.146
about the gap in my bracelet.

48:19.772 --> 48:22.190
I'm glad you'll give it back to me.

48:22.191 --> 48:24.193
- I'll see you tomorrow.
- All right.

48:25.319 --> 48:26.320
Bye.

48:29.865 --> 48:30.908
You're back.

48:36.705 --> 48:38.248
Yes, Mr. Park.

48:38.249 --> 48:40.792
Oh, I met Mr. Seonu in the lobby.

48:40.793 --> 48:42.128
Really?

48:42.795 --> 48:43.878
Okay.

48:43.879 --> 48:47.549
Grandma said
she wants to talk to you alone.

48:47.550 --> 48:48.967
Is that okay?

48:48.968 --> 48:51.887
- If you feel uncomfortable…
-  No, it's fine.

48:55.891 --> 48:58.810
I should have put more thought
into what you said that day.

48:58.811 --> 49:00.520
I'm sorry, Ms. Kim.

49:00.521 --> 49:01.938
"That day"?

49:01.939 --> 49:04.190
Thanks to you,
I'll be able to leave in peace.

49:04.191 --> 49:05.568
Are you going somewhere?

49:06.694 --> 49:09.697
I'm planning to stay in France
after I retire.

49:12.908 --> 49:15.035
I hid this on purpose.

49:15.661 --> 49:17.329
How could you have known?

49:19.498 --> 49:20.499
Are you all right?

49:21.083 --> 49:22.460
I'm fine.

49:24.086 --> 49:25.087
But…

49:25.629 --> 49:27.505
I'd like to ask you the same thing.

49:27.506 --> 49:28.924
I heard about your head.

49:30.134 --> 49:31.469
Are you sure you're okay?

49:33.012 --> 49:34.013
I'm fine.

49:34.930 --> 49:36.055
No,

49:36.056 --> 49:38.225
I'm going to make sure I'm fine

49:38.893 --> 49:41.145
so I can stay by Ms. Song's side.

49:42.021 --> 49:44.148
My head, and everything else…

49:46.692 --> 49:48.109
I'm going to make it all okay.

49:50.863 --> 49:51.864
Haran cares…

49:53.365 --> 49:55.200
for you a lot.

49:55.201 --> 49:58.287
It actually surprised me
how sincere she is about you.

49:58.913 --> 50:01.999
And she seems to be
thinking of a future with you.

50:03.250 --> 50:06.377
I know, and I feel the same way.

50:06.378 --> 50:07.755
I want to see you two

50:09.173 --> 50:11.634
getting along well for as long as I can.

50:12.885 --> 50:16.347
At least for Haran's sake and your sake,

50:17.848 --> 50:19.225
make sure you're okay.

50:23.062 --> 50:24.063
I will.

50:27.691 --> 50:29.400
Thanks for coming.

50:29.401 --> 50:32.070
Oh. When's your checkup again?

50:32.071 --> 50:33.154
Next week.

50:33.155 --> 50:35.365
It'll be fine, so don't worry about me.

50:35.366 --> 50:36.700
Take good care of Ms. Kim.

50:37.284 --> 50:38.368
I'll get going now.

50:38.369 --> 50:40.037
- Right, your cardigan.
- Ah…

50:41.038 --> 50:42.706
Keep it on. You'll catch a cold.

50:45.209 --> 50:46.418
Don't worry.

50:50.422 --> 50:51.882
Grandma was right.

50:53.008 --> 50:56.719
Having just one person to lean on

50:56.720 --> 50:58.097
will help you stay strong.

51:02.226 --> 51:04.936
I do have a pretty broad back.

51:04.937 --> 51:06.271
When did you notice?

51:06.272 --> 51:08.606
Should I leave my back here
for you to lean on?

51:10.943 --> 51:13.611
- Go.
- Okay. I'll go now.

51:13.612 --> 51:14.613
Bye.

51:18.158 --> 51:19.243
Head back inside.

51:39.513 --> 51:40.514
Let me talk to you.

51:41.807 --> 51:43.308
What do you think you're doing?

51:43.309 --> 51:45.018
Stop messing with her.

51:45.019 --> 51:46.687
The thing you wanted to protect…

51:48.230 --> 51:49.231
was her?

51:49.940 --> 51:52.318
Are you worried you'll lose her
if I say something?

51:53.319 --> 51:54.652
Does she know

51:54.653 --> 51:58.156
that you went to the same school
as Hyeokchan and were his roommate?

51:58.157 --> 51:59.158
Does she know who you are?

52:00.492 --> 52:03.286
Hyeokchan's dead, but you're alive,

52:03.287 --> 52:05.873
and the person you want to protect
is his old girlfriend?

52:07.041 --> 52:08.166
That's funny.

52:08.167 --> 52:09.250
Since when?

52:09.251 --> 52:11.002
Did you have feelings for her then?

52:11.003 --> 52:13.046
You must've jumped at the chance
when he died.

52:13.047 --> 52:14.839
Don't say it like that.

52:14.840 --> 52:16.216
That's not the case.

52:17.259 --> 52:20.262
She's going through a hard time right now.

52:20.888 --> 52:23.182
Don't say things that…

52:24.224 --> 52:25.683
will only dig up old wounds.

52:25.684 --> 52:27.185
Please.

52:27.186 --> 52:29.355
Why should I do that for you?

52:32.524 --> 52:33.692
I remembered something.

52:34.568 --> 52:36.153
The day that the waste container fell,

52:37.529 --> 52:39.364
you were in the lab as well.

52:39.365 --> 52:41.032
And you were shouting at him to stop.

52:44.078 --> 52:47.288
I don't have the time
to answer all your questions.

52:47.289 --> 52:49.875
Why was the waste container
next to Hyeokchan?

52:52.127 --> 52:54.253
The day Hyeokchan's lip was busted…

52:54.254 --> 52:55.339
Was that day

52:56.048 --> 52:58.008
the day of the accident?

52:59.218 --> 53:02.095
I didn't have any memories
of that day until now,

53:02.096 --> 53:04.097
but it feels like it's from that day.

53:04.098 --> 53:08.018
Tell me what happened in the lab that day.

53:09.395 --> 53:10.396
You know what happened.

53:12.106 --> 53:14.774
You can't tell Haran the truth.

53:14.775 --> 53:16.109
No, you're not telling her.

53:16.110 --> 53:18.820
So why are you so obsessed
with finding out what happened?

53:18.821 --> 53:21.280
If everyone involved
has the right to know,

53:21.281 --> 53:24.868
shouldn't Haran also know
that you're fake?

53:25.828 --> 53:27.370
I'm going to tell her.

53:27.371 --> 53:29.956
- But right now--
- If you go and tell her first,

53:29.957 --> 53:32.668
then I might think about telling you, too.

53:40.759 --> 53:41.926
Please.

53:41.927 --> 53:43.971
Stop asking me strange questions.

53:44.763 --> 53:46.139
If you provoke me,

53:46.140 --> 53:49.685
even I don't know
what I'll end up telling her.

53:57.651 --> 53:58.777
Hey, Kang Hyeokchan.

53:59.570 --> 54:01.195
I have to tell you something.

54:01.196 --> 54:04.699
I've been chatting with your girlfriend.

54:04.700 --> 54:06.452
She thinks she's been talking to you.

54:07.035 --> 54:08.286
You were pretending to be me?

54:08.287 --> 54:09.871
Do you have any idea what you've done?

54:11.206 --> 54:13.207
- I'm sorry.
-  Did you have feelings for her?

54:13.208 --> 54:14.917
You must've jumped at the chance.

54:14.918 --> 54:17.296
Shouldn't Haran also know
that you're fake?

54:22.801 --> 54:24.094
I told him…

54:24.678 --> 54:25.929
I told Hyeokchan everything.

54:26.764 --> 54:27.765
But…

54:29.099 --> 54:31.059
what happened after that?

54:46.116 --> 54:47.868
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

54:48.744 --> 54:50.037
It's all my fault.

54:51.038 --> 54:52.080
"Fault…"

54:59.171 --> 55:01.048
-  Nineteen.
- Nineteen.

55:01.632 --> 55:04.425
-  Thirty-one point five.
- Thirty-one point five.

55:04.426 --> 55:06.636
Everyone, let's keep our spirits up.

55:06.637 --> 55:08.513
When Ms. Kim comes back,

55:08.514 --> 55:11.557
we should show her how much we did
to put her mind at ease.

55:11.558 --> 55:13.684
So how about a quick cheer?

55:13.685 --> 55:15.437
No, forget it.

55:16.688 --> 55:18.773
One, two, three.

55:18.774 --> 55:20.025
Let's do this!

55:21.068 --> 55:22.318
Let's do this!

55:22.319 --> 55:23.569
Whatever it is.

55:23.570 --> 55:24.654
- Hey.
- It's Chan.

55:24.655 --> 55:26.697
What's the occasion?
There's no meeting today.

55:26.698 --> 55:28.991
We got the additional script,
so I dropped by.

55:28.992 --> 55:32.411
And since SHIM is closed,
I made these myself.

55:32.412 --> 55:33.538
I can't guarantee the taste.

55:33.539 --> 55:34.956
- Thank you.
-  Thank you.

55:34.957 --> 55:38.709
But Ms. Song isn't here right now.

55:38.710 --> 55:39.919
Really?

55:39.920 --> 55:42.505
- Where did she go?
- She took the afternoon off.

55:42.506 --> 55:46.300
Even if Ms. Kim told her not to come,
I guess she's pretty worried.

55:46.301 --> 55:47.718
Did she go to the hospital?

55:47.719 --> 55:50.179
No, she said she had to drop by somewhere.

55:50.180 --> 55:52.848
She had to return something to someone.

55:52.849 --> 55:53.850
Oh…

55:54.601 --> 55:56.060
And my bracelet…

55:56.061 --> 55:58.020
I'm glad you'll give it back to me.

55:58.021 --> 55:59.689
I'll see you tomorrow.

56:02.067 --> 56:06.530
Sunyul National
University Hospital is 1.5 km ahead.

56:10.701 --> 56:13.287
Does she know who you are?

56:16.206 --> 56:17.374
If you provoke me,

56:18.584 --> 56:22.296
even I don't know
what I'll end up telling her.

56:39.855 --> 56:43.357
Ah. The last patient's tone
seemed worse than the tremor.

56:43.358 --> 56:45.444
- Let's reduce the dose.
-  Okay, I'll check.

57:02.544 --> 57:04.795
- Oh. Haran.
-  You're here.

57:04.796 --> 57:08.049
Mr. Seonu's upstairs, right?
I have to give him something.

57:08.050 --> 57:09.718
He just left when I came here.

57:10.302 --> 57:11.761
He said he had to go somewhere.

57:11.762 --> 57:12.763
Oh…

57:13.597 --> 57:16.307
Then can I just leave this in his room?

57:16.308 --> 57:17.892
Sure, that's fine.

57:17.893 --> 57:21.228
I'm heading back to the hospital.
I just came to get my stuff.

57:21.229 --> 57:24.273
Then I'll give you a ride.
I'm heading there, too.

57:24.274 --> 57:26.108
No, it's fine. I called a cab.

57:26.109 --> 57:29.403
I made a lot of coffee
to share with the doctors.

57:29.404 --> 57:31.947
I'll leave one for you.

57:31.948 --> 57:35.034
Take your time drinking this
and meet Chan first.

57:35.035 --> 57:36.536
- Okay.
-  He'll be back soon.

57:38.288 --> 57:39.289
Mr. Park.

57:39.998 --> 57:41.082
Yes?

57:41.083 --> 57:43.585
Thank you for taking care of my grandma.

57:44.836 --> 57:46.672
Gosh.

57:47.422 --> 57:49.131
There's no need to thank me.

57:55.806 --> 57:58.558
TEMPORARILY CLOSED
SORRY FOR THE INCONVENIENCE

58:04.981 --> 58:07.067
Pardon me.

58:14.741 --> 58:16.660
SEONU CHAN

58:26.795 --> 58:27.921
Hey, roomie.

58:29.005 --> 58:30.214
Yes, she's here.

58:30.215 --> 58:32.384
She brought something for you,
so she went upstairs.

58:33.093 --> 58:34.802
Hang on.

58:34.803 --> 58:36.137
No, it's okay.

58:36.138 --> 58:37.847
I'll be there in a few minutes.

58:37.848 --> 58:39.140
Really?

58:39.141 --> 58:41.268
Huh? My cab's here.

58:41.768 --> 58:43.395
I'm going to the hospital,

58:43.895 --> 58:46.106
so take care of Genius for me.

58:48.900 --> 58:50.777
Is there a Post-it? Oh?

59:32.778 --> 59:33.779
Is she upstairs?

59:34.738 --> 59:35.906
Are you here?

59:37.532 --> 59:38.617
Huh?

59:42.579 --> 59:43.747
Hmm?

59:46.750 --> 59:48.084
THANKS FOR THE

01:00:22.536 --> 01:00:24.871
KANG HYEOKCHAN, GLASS TUBE, BLOOD
THAT SOUND AGAIN

01:00:34.673 --> 01:00:37.509
KANG HYEOKCHAN HOSPITALIZED, WOMAN
THAT SOUND WAS HER BRACELET

01:00:39.344 --> 01:00:41.595
I'll tell her everything

01:00:41.596 --> 01:00:43.056
and apologize to her.

01:00:44.057 --> 01:00:45.516
I want to tell her everything

01:00:45.517 --> 01:00:48.395
and love her as my true self…

01:00:49.980 --> 01:00:50.981
from now on.

01:00:51.857 --> 01:00:52.899
Before it's too late.

01:01:12.168 --> 01:01:13.586
Chan.

01:01:13.587 --> 01:01:15.045
Why did you come back?

01:01:15.046 --> 01:01:16.422
Well…

01:01:16.423 --> 01:01:19.049
Did Ms. Song come here?

01:01:19.050 --> 01:01:20.509
Hey, what's gotten into you?

01:01:20.510 --> 01:01:23.138
- We told you she's going to the hospital.
- Ah…

01:01:25.390 --> 01:01:26.391
All right.

01:01:29.185 --> 01:01:33.480
Mr. Park, is Ms. Song
at the hospital right now?

01:01:33.481 --> 01:01:35.357
No, she's not here.

01:01:35.358 --> 01:01:38.152
Did you not see her?

01:01:38.153 --> 01:01:39.195
Oh…

01:01:40.196 --> 01:01:41.573
It's nothing. Never mind.

01:01:59.883 --> 01:02:02.010
RAN

01:02:08.224 --> 01:02:09.767
Are you home?

01:02:09.768 --> 01:02:11.310
If you're home, come out.

01:02:11.311 --> 01:02:13.437
Let's meet. Let's meet up and talk.

01:02:13.438 --> 01:02:14.856
I'll explain everything.

01:02:53.728 --> 01:02:55.313
- Hey…
-  Don't come any closer.

01:03:04.531 --> 01:03:06.074
Boston Institute of Technology.

01:03:07.617 --> 01:03:09.327
Kang Hyeokchan's roommate.

01:03:10.787 --> 01:03:12.163
Have you really known me

01:03:13.289 --> 01:03:15.000
for seven years?

01:03:21.172 --> 01:03:22.841
- Song Haran.
- Don't say my name.

01:03:26.052 --> 01:03:27.303
Did you have fun

01:03:28.596 --> 01:03:30.223
pretending to be Kang Hyeokchan?

01:03:41.735 --> 01:03:43.695
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:04:07.802 --> 01:04:10.888
She found out about everything.

01:04:10.889 --> 01:04:12.639
I didn't have the chance to explain.

01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:14.517
If those two facts don't change,

01:04:15.226 --> 01:04:16.311
I won't change, either.

01:04:17.187 --> 01:04:18.896
Don't ever show up in front of me again.

01:04:18.897 --> 01:04:22.150
You don't have to look at me
or listen to me. So please,

01:04:22.901 --> 01:04:24.526
just look at this.

01:04:24.527 --> 01:04:27.029
Haran, you're burning up.

01:04:27.030 --> 01:04:29.740
You did a great job so far
working by my side.

01:04:29.741 --> 01:04:31.742
Haran's gone.

01:04:31.743 --> 01:04:34.244
You're the only one I could ask
where she could be.

01:04:34.245 --> 01:04:36.455
I have to go find her.

01:04:36.456 --> 01:04:38.458
It has to be me.

01:04:50.470 --> 01:04:51.553
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:04:51.554 --> 01:04:52.555
Translated by Juyoung Park
